Theorem PL-1: interprocedural-first — Steps 1-2 run once across all functions before any per-function step

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered sequence per
      Annex E §AIMS §6. Steps partition into
      an INTERPROCEDURAL prefix (Steps 1-2, run ONCE across the whole
      program) and a PER-FUNCTION suffix (Steps 3-12, run per function):
        Step 1: analyze_program() — MemoryContract per fn (SCC fixpoint)
        Step 2: apply_ownership() — ArcParam.ownership from contracts
        Step 3: compute_var_reprs() — ValueRepr per variable
        Step 3a: normalize_function() — TRMC context region detection
        Step 4: analyze_function() — backward dataflow -> AimsStateMap
        Step 4a: verify_trmc_soundness()
        Step 5: realize_rc_reuse() — RC + reuse (pre-merge)
        Step 5a: verify_fip_contract()
        Step 6: verify()
        Step 7: run_aims_verify()
        Step 8: detect/rewrite tail calls
        Step 8a: unwind_cleanup()
        Step 9: merge_blocks()
        Step 10: realize_annotations() — COW + drop hints (post-merge)
        Step 11: verify()
        Step 12: FBIP enforcement
    - PL-1 statement (per Annex E §AIMS PL-1 + Annex E §AIMS §6
      "Interprocedural (once)" header): Steps 1-2 SHALL run once across
      ALL functions before ANY per-function step (3-12) runs on ANY
      function.
    - PL-1 type signature (per Pipeline.proof lines 15-18, the sorry
      obligation this theorem discharges):
        type : List FunctionId -> Pipeline
        Steps 1-2 (analyze_program + apply_ownership) SHALL run once
        across all functions before any per-function step (3-12).
    - Shipped pipeline driver: ori_arc::pipeline::run_arc_pipeline_all
      (compiler/ori_arc/src/pipeline/mod.rs lines 120-140)
      delegates to ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::run_aims_pipeline_all
      (compiler/ori_arc/src/pipeline/aims_pipeline/batch.rs
      lines 31-84). The batch driver executes:
        (a) Step 1 — analyze_program(functions, ...) ONCE over the whole
            `functions` slice (batch.rs line 44; computes MemoryContract
            for every function via SCC fixpoint);
        (b) Step 2 — apply_aims_ownership(functions, &contracts) ONCE
            over the whole slice (batch.rs line 50);
        (c) THEN the per-function loop `for func in functions.iter_mut()`
            (batch.rs line 74) calls super::run_aims_pipeline(func, ...)
            (batch.rs line 75) — the Steps 3-12 per-function pipeline at
            ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::run_aims_pipeline
            (compiler/ori_arc/src/pipeline/aims_pipeline/mod.rs
            lines 163-221: Steps 3-3a normalize_with_trmc, Step 4
            analyze_function, Step 4a verify_trmc_soundness, Step 5
            realize_rc_reuse).
    - The interprocedural prefix is the ANTECEDENT of every per-function
      step: Step 4 (analyze_function) reads the MemoryContract map
      produced by Step 1 (run_aims_pipeline takes `config.contracts`,
      mod.rs line 187) and Step 2 populates ArcParam.ownership the
      per-function realization consumes. Running any per-function step
      before Steps 1-2 completes would read an absent/incomplete contract
      map — a sequencing bug per Annex E §AIMS PL-5 "no pass relies
      on stale summaries".
    - This theorem reasons over the LINEAR 12-step pipeline DAG (Step k
      precedes Step k+1), distinct from PL-1a whose induction domain is
      the program call-graph SCC DAG. PL-1 fixes the PREFIX/SUFFIX
      boundary (Steps 1-2 before 3-12); PL-1a fixes the ORDER within the
      per-function suffix's function iteration.

  Soundness property:
    Forall program PROG = (List FunctionId), let pipeline P be the
    shipped run_aims_pipeline_all schedule on PROG.
      Two conjuncts SHALL hold:

      (P1) Prefix-runs-once:
        Steps 1 and 2 each execute EXACTLY ONCE over the whole-program
        function slice, before the per-function loop begins. There is no
        execution point at which Step 1 or Step 2 runs a second time, and
        no per-function step (3-12) precedes the single completion of
        Steps 1-2.

      (P2) Prefix-before-suffix:
        For every function F in PROG and every per-function step k in
        {3, 3a, 4, 4a, 5, 5a, 6, 7, 8, 8a, 9, 10, 11, 12}:
          completion(Step 2 over PROG) precedes start(step k on F).
        Equivalently: in the total execution order, the position of the
        last interprocedural step (Step 2) is strictly less than the
        position of the first per-function step on any F.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part constructive discharge corresponding to (P1) and (P2), by
    structural induction over the 12-step pipeline DAG (linear chain
    Step 1 -> ... -> Step 12) + case analysis on the prefix/suffix
    partition boundary.

    Part (P1) — Prefix-runs-once (structural induction over the prefix):

      Base case — Step 1 (analyze_program):
        run_aims_pipeline_all (batch.rs lines 31-84) calls
        crate::aims::interprocedural::analyze_program(functions, ...)
        at line 44 in a single straight-line statement — no loop, no
        recursion. analyze_program (scc_driver.rs lines 33-104) takes the
        whole `functions: &[ArcFunction]` slice and returns one
        FxHashMap<Name, MemoryContract>. It executes once per
        run_aims_pipeline_all invocation. Post-condition: a complete
        contract map for every function in PROG exists.

      Inductive step — Step 2 (apply_ownership) follows Step 1, once:
        Immediately after Step 1's statement, batch.rs line 50 calls
        apply_aims_ownership(functions, &contracts) once over the whole
        slice. The `&contracts` argument is precisely Step 1's output —
        Step 2 consumes Step 1's post-condition. No loop wraps Steps 1-2.
        Post-condition: ArcParam.ownership populated for every function.

      Termination of the prefix:
        Steps 1-2 are two straight-line statements (batch.rs lines 44, 50)
        with no surrounding control flow. They run exactly once each. The
        prefix completes before any later statement executes (sequential
        Rust statement evaluation). (P1) discharged.

    Part (P2) — Prefix-before-suffix (case analysis on the partition):

      The per-function suffix is the loop `for func in functions.iter_mut()`
      at batch.rs line 74, whose body calls super::run_aims_pipeline(func,
      &config) (line 75). This loop is the FIRST statement after Step 2's
      line 50 (the AimsPipelineConfig construction at lines 54-64 is pure
      data assembly carrying `contracts: &contracts` — Step 1's output —
      with no pipeline-step side effect).

      Case analysis on each per-function step k in run_aims_pipeline
      (mod.rs lines 163-221):
        Case k = Step 3/3a (normalize_with_trmc, mod.rs line 169):
          Reaches only inside the loop body, which the for-loop header at
          line 74 gates behind Step 2's completion. start(Step 3 on F) >
          completion(Step 2 over PROG).
        Case k = Step 4 (analyze_function, mod.rs line 184):
          Takes `config.contracts` (mod.rs line 187) = Step 1's contract
          map. The map is fully populated by Step 1's single execution
          BEFORE the loop. start(Step 4 on F) > completion(Step 1).
        Case k = Step 4a..Step 12 (verify_trmc_soundness onward):
          Each is a statement strictly after Step 4 within
          run_aims_pipeline's body; transitively each starts after the
          loop header, hence after Step 2.
      In every case, the per-function step on any F starts strictly after
      the single completion of Steps 1-2. (P2) discharged.

    Coverage gate — pipeline-step partition enumeration:

      The verifier enumerates the 14-step shipped schedule (12 numbered
      steps plus the 3a/4a/5a/8a sub-steps that the linear chain
      threads) partitioned into:
        Prefix (interprocedural, run-once): {1, 2}
        Suffix (per-function): {3, 3a, 4, 4a, 5, 5a, 6, 7,
                                              8, 8a, 9, 10, 11, 12}
      and discharges, for every suffix step s, the ordering predicate
      position(Step 2) < position(s). It also asserts |prefix| = 2 and
      that the prefix members carry the run-once attribute (no enclosing
      loop), matching the shipped batch.rs straight-line Steps 1-2 vs the
      `for func` per-function loop.

      Coverage axes:
        Prefix-runs-once (P1): the 2 prefix steps {1, 2} verified to be
          loop-free straight-line statements (batch.rs 44, 50).
        Prefix-before-suffix (P2): all 14 suffix steps verified to follow
          Step 2 in the total order.

    Negative-direction witness — suffix-step-before-prefix rejected:

      Hypothetically scheduling Step 4 (analyze_function) before Step 1
      (analyze_program) would have analyze_function read an EMPTY contract
      map (config.contracts unpopulated). Per the dependency at mod.rs
      line 187, Step 4 consumes `config.contracts`; an unpopulated map
      yields conservative-everywhere contracts, silently degrading every
      downstream RC/reuse decision and violating Annex E §AIMS PL-5
      ("no pass relies on stale summaries" — here, an ABSENT summary). The
      verifier rejects any partition placing a suffix step at a position
      <= position(Step 2).

    Negative-direction witness — prefix-runs-twice rejected:

      Re-running Step 1 inside the per-function loop (once per function)
      would recompute the whole-program SCC fixpoint N times for N
      functions, and — worse — each re-run would overwrite the contract
      map mid-iteration, so a function realized early would see different
      callee contracts than a function realized late: a stale-summary
      hazard per PL-5. The shipped driver runs Step 1 exactly once
      (batch.rs line 44, outside the loop); the verifier rejects any
      schedule with prefix-step multiplicity > 1.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-1 has no upstream pipeline dependency:

      PL-1 fixes the FIRST boundary in the pipeline order (prefix before
      suffix). Steps 1-2 consume only lowered ArcFunctions (the output of
      ARC lowering,  sec-1 phase 5) — no later pipeline step's
      output. The dependency chain is acyclic at the proof-obligation
      level:
        PL-1 --> PL-1a (per-function SCC topological order within the
                          suffix loop)
        PL-1 --> PL-2 (Step 4 precedes Step 5 within each F)
        PL-1 --> PL-3/PL-4/PL-4a (later intra-F step boundaries)
        PL-1 + PL-1a --> PL-5 (no stale summaries — depends on both the
                          prefix-once guarantee and the callee-first order)
      PL-1 is a leaf of this dependency tree.

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      property: pipeline-prefix/suffix ordering (interprocedural
                           Steps 1-2 run once before per-function Steps 3-12)
      published: standard compiler-pass-ordering discipline; the
                           "whole-program analysis before per-function
                           transformation" shape matches Lean 4
                           src/Lean/Compiler/IR (collect_O whole-program
                           pass before per-decl RC insertion) cited in
                           the published reference-compiler corpus
      determinism: deterministic given a deterministic function
                           iteration order; the shipped slice
                           `functions: &[ArcFunction]` preserves insertion
                           order per Annex E §AIMS PL-5 
                           sec-1 phase purity
      reference impl: ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::
                           run_aims_pipeline_all (batch.rs lines 31-84:
                           Step 1 line 44, Step 2 line 50, per-function
                           loop line 74)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — structural induction over the linear
        12-step pipeline DAG per section_07::verify_pl1_interprocedural_first;
        the verifier enumerates the prefix/suffix partition and discharges
        (P1) prefix-runs-once via the loop-free straight-line attribute on
        Steps 1-2 and (P2) prefix-before-suffix via the position-ordering
        predicate position(Step 2) < position(s) for every suffix step s;
        emits Fail on any partition violation)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — per-step precondition case grid over the
        14 suffix steps; gracious-accept once structural_induction has
        discharged the ordering obligation per the coverage-manifest PL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 structural_induction engine discharges PL-1 via the prefix/suffix pipeline-DAG partition — (P1) Steps 1-2 run once as loop-free straight-line statements (batch.rs 44/50) and (P2) every per-function step (3-12) follows Step 2 in the total order; grounded in the shipped run_aims_pipeline_all driver (batch.rs lines 31-84) where analyze_program + apply_ownership precede the `for func` per-function loop, with case_analysis secondary-accepting per the coverage-manifest PL row
